    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1338">

                <pb facs="1596" n="1398" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1398"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/7–1845: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1338<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Deputy Director of the Office of Near
                        Eastern and African Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Allen</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Director of Near Eastern and African Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Henderson</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1338-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-18">July 18, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 82.
                    To Acting Secretary of State for Loy
                        Henderson from George
                        Allen.</p>
                <p>Sent to Department. Repeated to Paris and Tangier for Villard and Ailing.</p>
                <p>Russians have proposed addition of Tangier and the Levant states to the agenda
                    for the conference.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1338-f2"/></p>
                <p>There is, as yet, no indication of Russian attitude regarding either
                    question.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1338-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1338-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the Acting Secretary of State over the signature of Byrnes.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1338-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1338-f2-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg46">pp. 46</ref>, <ref
